# Known divergences (by design):
# - foreign-data wrapper/server/table operations are blocked through the pooler,
#   so dependent extended-statistics checks and cleanup output differ.
# - the check_estimated_rows helper runs a dynamic EXECUTE the pooler cannot vet,
#   so its runtime CREATE is rejected. It is pre-seeded on the primary
#   (testdata/pg17/regress_preseed.sql) so the estimation checks still run; the
#   remaining reject is the inline CREATE STATISTICS DO block (not a reusable
#   function to seed).
--- a
+++ b
@@ -24,6 +24,7 @@
 end loop;
 end;
 $$;
+ERROR: EXECUTE of a runtime-built statement inside a PL/pgSQL body is not supported: the statement text is not a constant, so it cannot be checked for unsafe session-state changes
